! mcp_bootstrap_p178.strap -- THE PSEUDO-OP BRANCH TABLE, printed
! page 178.  Three dispatch legs of the I-O service-op dispatcher --
! KOPOK, KPLUG1 and KCOP -- and the fifty-one branch entries they
! index into.
!
! docs/MCP_Mar63_001-249.pdf PDF p.185.  The header was RENDERED and
! READ, not assumed: "TIME CLOCK 00054041  PUNID 11D11MCP   CARD ID
! LA000056   DIST. OF 3/01   3/01   PAGE NUMBER  178".
!
! >>> THE COLUMN-HEADING ROW'S OWN "LOCATION" FIELD READS 220742. <<<
! It is NOT blank on this page.  That is IBM's own assembler stating
! line 1's location, and line 1's LOCATION column reads 220742.00, so
! the two agree.  Per docs/transcription_workflow.md the field is
! line 1's location and is blank only when line 1 compiles nothing;
! line 1 here is a located full-word VFL store, so a number is what
! the reading predicts and a number is what is there.
!
! ---------------------------------------------------------------
! WHAT THE PAGE IS
! ---------------------------------------------------------------
! FIFTY-SIX PRINTED LINES, every one of them located and emitting.
! No banner, no comment card, no DD, no SYN, no VF, no reservation,
! and NO SLC of any kind.  The page is CONTIGUOUS from 220742.00 to
! 220776.00 with no hole: fifty-four half words and one full word
! (line 1), and the counter leaves the page at 220776.40.
!
! COUNTED OFF THE CARD-SERIAL COLUMN, not off the survey.  The
! serials run LA000056 ... LA000110 -- fifty-five serials for
! fifty-six lines, the one repeat being LA000101 on lines 46 AND 47
! (see THE CARD SERIALS below).  NOTHING FELL OFF EITHER END:
! serial LA000056 is on line 1, LA000110 is on line 56, and line 56
! is followed by blank paper to the foot of the form.
!
! >>> WHERE THE SURVEY WENT WRONG, AND IT WENT WRONG AT BOTH ENDS.
! The cached survey gave this page as 220743.00 .. 220766.40.  Both
! endpoints are wrong and the row count is short by more than
! twenty:
!     survey first   220743.00   ACTUAL  220742.00   (line 1, lost)
!     survey last    220766.40   ACTUAL  220776.00   (ten words out)
! Line 1 is the page's only full word and the survey dropped it; the
! last endpoint is a plain misread of 220776 as 220766.  Both
! numbers here were counted off the page's own LINE and card-serial
! columns and both are confirmed independently -- see THE JOINS.
!
!   line  1       the tail of the previous page's work: a full-word
!                 VFL store of the control word, the ONLY full word
!                 on the page.  Carries a location-column asterisk.
!
!   lines  2-4    KOPOK, the main entry.  V+I,2,2.0 steps the
!                 calling-sequence pointer, SV,2,STIC plants the
!                 return address, and BR,-1.0($3) indexes the table
!                 below by the pseudo-op code in $3.
!
!   lines  5-30   THE $OP TABLE, twenty-six half-word branches at
!                 pseudo-op displacements 1.0 through 13.32.  Its
!                 comment column is the pseudo-op dictionary:
!                 -READ, -RELEASE, -LOCATE - DISK ONLY, -FEED CARD
!                 - PUNCH ONLY, -TAPE INDICATOR OFF ROUTINE,
!                 -INVALID OP, -ERASE LONG GAP, -SPACE BLOCK,
!                 -BACKSPACE BLOCK, -SPACE FILE, -WRITE TAPE MARK,
!                 -REWIND, -REWIND AND UNLOAD, -RESERVED LIGHT OFF
!                 ROUTINE, -RESERVED LIGHT ON ROUTINE, -CHECK LIGHT
!                 ON ROUTINE, -FREE REEL AND DRIVE, -SOUND GONG -
!                 CONSOLE ONLY, -WAIT FOR I/O INTERRUPT, -CHANGE
!                 I/O TABLE OF EXITS, -UNASSIGN TAPE UNIT.
!
!   lines 31-33   KPLUG1, the second leg.  KVI,3,37.32 bounds the
!                 code, BXH,MOPCI rejects anything higher, and
!                 BR,-32.0($3) indexes the table below.
!
!   lines 34-45   THE $OPS TABLE, twelve half-word branches at
!                 displacements 32.0 through 37.32: -STACK I/O
!                 INTERRUPTS, -RELEASE I/O INTERRUPTS, -RETURN
!                 AFTER I/O INTERRUPT, -RETURN AFTER MASKABLE,
!                 -STORE IN COMMUNICATION REGION, -FETCH FROM
!                 COMMUNICATION REGION, -SET INTERVAL TIMER.
!
!   lines 46-48   KCOP, the third leg.  KVI,3,16.32 / BXH,MOPCI /
!                 BR,-11.32($3).  Carries a location-column
!                 asterisk.
!
!   lines 49-56   the head of KCOP's table, displacements 11.32
!                 through 15.0.  It RUNS OFF THE BOTTOM OF THE PAGE
!                 and continues on printed p.179 -- see THE FORWARD
!                 JOIN, which names the three rows that follow.
!
! ---------------------------------------------------------------
! >>> THE DECISIVE WITNESS FOR THIS PAGE IS A TYPESET TABLE IN
!     C22-6728, AND IT MATCHES THE BRANCH TABLE ENTRY FOR ENTRY. <<<
! ---------------------------------------------------------------
! docs/ocr/C22-6728_7030_MCP_Sys_Analysis_Guide.txt and its -1
! revision both print "Routines are:" tables of Pseudo-Op / Entry
! Symbol for exactly these legs.  Different press, different ink,
! genuinely independent of this listing drum -- the workflow's
! glyph-ladder rung 2, and here it fires on twenty-eight names at
! once.  The -1 revision's $OPS table, reproduced as the OCR gives
! it:
!
!   $RD or $RDS 1.0  ZSTART    $RLF    9.0   BRLFR
!   $W or $WS   1.32 EWR1      $RLN    9.32  BRLNR
!   $CCW        2.0  BCCWR     $KLN   10.0   BKLNR
!   $REL        2.32 WREL      $FREE  10.32  ZFREE
!   $LOC        3.0  KSLOC     $GONG  11.0   WGONG
!   $FC         3.32 WFC       $WAIT  11.32  KWAIT
!   $TIF        4.0  BTIFR     $CHEX  12.0   CCHEX
!   (Invalid)   4.32 SDISP     $FREE  12.32  ZFREE
!   $ERG        5.0  EELG      $IODEF 13.0   JZIOR
!   $SP         5.32 R1        $HD    14.0   *RHD
!   $BSP        6.0  R1+1.0    $LD    14.32  *RLD
!   $SPFL       6.32 R1+2.0    $EVEN  15.0   *REVEN
!   $BSFL       7.0  R2-.32    $ODD   15.32  *RODD
!   $WEF        7.32 EWT1      $ECC   16.0   *RECC
!   $REW        8.0  ZREWST    $NOECC 16.32  *RNOECC
!   $UNLD       8.32 ZUNLDB    $ATID  17.0   SCBALT
!
!   $SIO  32.0  KSIO    $COMM  35.32 JCOMM
!   $RIO  32.32 KRIO    $SIT   36.0  JSITX
!   $RET  33.0  CRETN   $FIXUP 36.32 *SCBTT
!   $RAM  33.32 WRAMPP  $STLR  37.0  TSTLR
!   $STRG 34.0  KSTRG   $FELR  37.32 TFCHLR
!   $FECRG 34.32 KFECRG $ABEX  38.0  YABEX
!   $TIME 35.0  ZTIME
!
!   "* KCOP gives control to the location as indicated; however,
!    each routine resets $3 to 13.32 and control goes to RALLPS to
!    do functions common to the mode and density operations."
!
! Map that onto the page and it is line for line.  THE BRANCH-
! RELATIVE ARITHMETIC IS EXACT, and it is the page's own internal
! check: BR,addr($3) lands at the NEXT half word plus addr plus $3.
!     line  4  BR,-1.0($3)    next = 220744.40, so $3 = 1.0 lands on
!              line 5 and $3 = 13.32 lands on line 30 -- twenty-six
!              entries, lines 5-30, exactly the manual's 1.0..13.32
!     line 33  BR,-32.0($3)   next = 220763.00, so $3 = 32.0 lands
!              on line 34 and $3 = 37.32 on line 45 -- twelve
!              entries, exactly the manual's 32.0..37.32, which is
!              also exactly the bound KVI,3,37.32 sets
!     line 48  BR,-11.32($3)  next = 220772.40, so $3 = 11.32 lands
!              on line 49 and $3 = 16.32 on 220777.40 -- the bound
!              KVI,3,16.32 sets
! And the manual's footnote names line 30: displacement 13.32 is
! B,RALLPS, which is what the footnote says every asterisked
! routine returns through.
!
! >>> WHERE THE MANUAL DRIFTS FROM THIS LISTING, SO THAT NOBODY
!     DOWNSTREAM OVER-TRUSTS IT.  Three places, all recorded:
!   (i)  $FIXUP 36.32 is "*SCBTT" in the -1 revision; THIS LISTING
!        prints B,FFXP and printed p.174 DEFINES FFXP at 220560.00.
!        The -1 footnote explains it -- "For core storage
!        conservation, $FIXUP has been setup as a major package in
!        the 22 $DUMP leg" -- so the manual is describing a LATER
!        build.  The listing wins for the listing.
!   (ii) (Invalid) 4.32 is "SDISP (type 2)"; this listing prints
!        B,M OP CI.  No conflict, a difference of level: printed
!        p.119 DEFINES MOPCI as "LVI,14,SOPCI  - ILLEGAL OP CODE"
!        and printed p.117 calls it "Type 2 (MOPCI) illegal op
!        code", so MOPCI is the entry that sets error code 2 and
!        goes on to SDISP.  The manual names the destination.
!   (iii) THE BASE REVISION'S TABLES ARE SHORTER.  C22-6728 (no -1)
!        stops the $OP table at 13.0 JZIOR with no 13.32 entry and
!        no asterisked 14.0-17.0 leg at all, and stops the $OPS
!        table at 36.0 JSITX.  Its prose says "A pseudo-op code
!        greater than 13.0 is detected at this point".  THIS MARCH
!        1963 LISTING HAS BOTH EXTENSIONS, so on this point it sits
!        between the two revisions and the -1 table is the one that
!        matches it.  Use -1 for this page, not the base.
!
! ---------------------------------------------------------------
! >>> THE BACKWARD JOIN IS CLOSED, AND IT IS NOT CLOSED BY AN SLC.
! ---------------------------------------------------------------
! This page prints no SLC, so the "SLC, (8)220742.0" below is an
! ASSERTION, not a check (workflow, WHAT THE ORACLE CANNOT SEE item
! 2: a hard SLC overrides the arriving counter silently; all
! fifty-six !CHECK rows would move together and still pass).  What
! closes the join is three independent things:
!   (a) line 1's own printed LOCATION, 220742.00;
!   (b) THE HEADING ROW'S "LOCATION 220742", IBM's assembler saying
!       the same number a second time in a different place on the
!       same page;
!   (c) printed p.177's last line.  Its PDF p.184 is another
!       transcriber's page and nothing of it is transcribed here,
!       but the volume OCR indexes it as line 56 at 220741.00,
!       "CCOCCC4.22 8D .007000.20 CO  STC EU,7),SCCWH18($13)" -- a
!       FULL word at 220741.00, so the counter leaves p.177 at
!       220742.00.  NOTE THE PAIR IS NOT A DUPLICATE: p.177's card
!       is ST(BU,7),S CCW+.18($13) and prints 000004.22, this
!       page's line 1 is ST(BU,7),S CW+.18($13) and prints
!       000003.22.  SCW is 3.0 (printed p.102 line 14) and SCCW is
!       4.0; the two differ by one word and the listing prints the
!       difference.  Anyone merging the two pages should expect two
!       adjacent full words, not one card printed twice.
!
! ---------------------------------------------------------------
! >>> THE FORWARD JOIN, AND A PREDICTION THAT IS ALREADY HALF
!     CHECKED. <<<
! ---------------------------------------------------------------
! Line 56 is a HALF WORD at 220776.00, so THE COUNTER LEAVES THIS
! PAGE AT 220776.40.  The manual's KCOP leg continues $ODD 15.32 ->
! RODD, $ECC 16.0 -> RECC, $NOECC 16.32 -> RNOECC, and
! BR,-11.32($3) puts those at 220776.40, 220777.00 and 220777.40
! exactly.  So printed p.179's first three located rows MUST be
!     220776.40  B,RODD
!     220777.00  B,RECC
!     220777.40  B,RNOECC
! and its fourth row must be a NEW ROUTINE at 221000.00, because
! KVI,3,16.32 bounds this table at 16.32 and the manual's $ATID
! 17.0 SCBALT entry is therefore NOT in this build.
!
! CHECKED AGAINST THE VOLUME OCR OF PDF p.186, which is an INDEX of
! another page and not a witness for this one: it reads "1* 220776.4C
! 220235.50 CO B,RCDD", "2* 220777.CC 220340.10 CO B,RECC", "2%
! 220777.4C 220342.1C CO B,RNGECC", "4% 221C0C.0O0 C0CC14.47 C4 KOR
! KV 3 S FREE".  All four hold, including the new routine at
! 221000.00.  p.179's transcriber should treat this as a prediction
! to CHECK off their own ink, not as a reading -- the OCR mangles
! every one of those labels, and RODD/RECC/RNOECC are three more
! symbols this page needs from them.
!
! ---------------------------------------------------------------
! WHAT PRINTED p.177's TRANSCRIBER NEEDS FROM HERE
! ---------------------------------------------------------------
! THIS PAGE DEFINES THREE SYMBOLS p.177 BRANCHES TO, and the volume
! OCR garbles all three names:
!     KOPOK    220743.00   this page's line 2  (OCR of p.177 line 49
!                          reads "BXE,K OP GK -> 220743.32 02")
!     KPLUG1   220761.40   this page's line 31 (OCR of p.177 line 11
!                          reads "BZXL,K PLUGI -> 220761.72 40")
!     KCOP     220771.00   this page's line 46 (OCR of p.177 line 43
!                          reads "BZXL,K C CP -> 220771.32 40")
! All three half words are consistent with the locations printed
! here, and p.177 should SYN them at those values.
!
! ---------------------------------------------------------------
! >>> THE NAME CALLS.  THE OCR GARBLES THIS PAGE'S NAMES BADLY AND
!     THIS IS THE FIRST FIRST-HAND READING OF THEM. <<<
! ---------------------------------------------------------------
! (1) >>> THE ENTRY IS "K OP OK" = KOPOK, NOT KCPOK, AND THE DECK
!     THAT WROTE KCPOK WOULD HAVE BEEN WRONG. <<<  At 1200 dpi the
!     NAME field of line 2 prints K, blank, [open round], P, blank,
!     [closed O], K -- which reads "K CP OK" to the eye.  Three
!     independent things say the second glyph is an O:
!       (a) THE SAME STATEMENT PRINTED THREE TIMES ON THIS PAGE,
!           which is the workflow's strongest rung.  Lines 49, 50
!           and 52 are the same card, "B,KOPOK", all three
!           compiling 220743.10.  In the FOURTH character position
!           line 50 prints a CLOSED O and lines 49 and 52 print it
!           OPEN -- one page, one drum, one instruction, the same
!           character position, varying only the ink.  So an open
!           round glyph in this name is an O that lost its right
!           stroke, demonstrated on this page by this name.
!       (b) THE TYPESET MANUAL.  C22-6728 prints KOPOK six times
!           and C22-6728-1 six more, in running prose -- "control
!           is given to KOPOK to accomplish the entry", "may be
!           entered immediately via KOPOK", "the return address
!           (KOPOK)".  The single "KCPOK" hit in -1 is inside an
!           ASCII flow-chart box whose counterpart in the base
!           revision reads KOPOK, i.e. one OCR slip of the same
!           box.  Twelve to one, across two revisions, different
!           press.
!       (c) printed p.177's line 49 and printed p.179's line 15,
!           both branches to 220743.00 from OTHER pages, OCR as
!           "BXE,K OP GK" and "BXE,K GP CK" -- O in the second
!           position in both.
!     docs/archival_inventory_notes.md already lists KOPOK in this
!     repository's own symbol inventory; nothing anywhere in the
!     repository spells it KCPOK (grepped repo-wide, not just
!     decks/).
!
! (2) "KCOP" ON LINE 46 IS K-C-O-P AND THE C IS A REAL C.  Read at
!     1200 dpi against line 2's name in the same column: line 2's
!     damaged O has a STRAIGHT VERTICAL LEFT STEM with square
!     corners, and line 46's second glyph is ROUND on the left with
!     no stem -- the workflow's C/D/O discriminator, applied within
!     one column of one page.  Line 46's THIRD glyph does have the
!     stem and is an O.  C22-6728-1 prints "KCOP" in prose in the
!     footnote quoted above, which is the independent confirmation.
!     KCOP is NOT the same symbol as KCOPY (printed p.122 line 45,
!     215744.00); they differ by a letter and by 1025 words.
!
! (3) "B,B CCW R" ON LINE 7 IS BCCWR, not "B COW R".  printed p.157
!     DEFINES BCCWR at 217766.00, which is the word this row
!     prints, and the manual's table gives $CCW 2.0 -> BCCWR.
!
! (4) "B,K SIO"/"B,K RIO" ON LINES 34/35 ARE KSIO AND KRIO.  The
!     volume OCR reads "K STO" and similar; printed p.170 DEFINES
!     both ("printed K SIC / K RIC" in that deck's own note) at
!     220410.40 and 220415.00, the two words these rows print, and
!     the manual gives $SIO 32.0 KSIO, $RIO 32.32 KRIO.
!
! (5) "B,K STRG"/"B,K FECRG" ON LINES 38/39 ARE KSTRG AND KFECRG.
!     The volume OCR reads "K STRGE"; printed p.171 DEFINES both at
!     220427.40 and 220445.40 and the manual gives $STRG 34.0
!     KSTRG, $FECRG 34.32 KFECRG.  Three readings, one answer.
!
! (6) "B,B KLN R" ON LINE 23 IS BKLNR with a K, and its own comment
!     says so: "-CHECK LIGHT ON ROUTINE".  Compare lines 21 and 22,
!     BRLFR and BRLNR, "-RESERVED LIGHT OFF/ON ROUTINE".  The
!     manual gives $KLN 10.0 BKLNR.
!
! (7) "B,MCPCI" ON LINE 53 IS MOPCI.  Same name as lines 12 and 32,
!     which print it with blanks as "M OP CI"; all three compile
!     215630 and printed p.119 DEFINES MOPCI at 215630.40.  On line
!     53 the SECOND glyph is an open O and the FOURTH is a genuine
!     C -- the two cases side by side in one name, which is the
!     workflow's "ink varies per CHARACTER, not per row" with a
!     worked example.
!
! (8) THE SAME NAME IS PRINTED WITH AND WITHOUT ITS BLANKS ON THIS
!     ONE PAGE.  Line 2 is "K OP OK" and lines 49/50/52 are
!     "KOPOK"; line 12 is "M OP CI" and line 53 is "MOPCI"; line 32
!     is "BXH,M OP CI" and line 47 is "BXH,MOPCI".  Each pair
!     compiles the identical word, which is this page's own proof
!     that STRAP ignores blanks inside a symbol.  Recorded so that
!     a later reader does not "correct" one spelling towards the
!     other.
!
! ---------------------------------------------------------------
! THE ONE BYTE THE INK GOT WRONG, AND WHAT SETTLED IT
! ---------------------------------------------------------------
! LINE 1's SECOND HALF WORD IS "007000.20 D0", NOT "...C0".  At 400
! and 600 dpi the byte reads C0, and the page drops ink on round
! glyphs constantly -- line 1's own octal fields print "COCCO3.22"
! and "0C7000.2C", five impossible Cs in fields that can hold only
! octal digits, so the row demonstrably drops ink.  Per the
! workflow that licenses nothing by itself.  What settles it is the
! LEFT SIDE at 1200 dpi, rendered beside the D of this same row's
! "8D" two inches away: both glyphs have a STRAIGHT VERTICAL LEFT
! STEM with square top-left and bottom-left corners and a bowl hung
! off it, and the byte's bowl is worn through on the right.  A C
! and a 0 are round on the left with no stem, and the "0" that
! follows in the same byte is exactly that.  This is the workflow's
! C-vs-D pair, the one it calls the worst.  The assembler agrees
! independently: ST(BU,7),SCW+.18($13) compiles 000003.22 8D
! 007000.20 D0, and it was the ONLY one of the page's fifty-six
! rows where the first reading and the assembler disagreed.
!
! Every other doubtful glyph on the page is a round one in a
! position where the assembler and the printed octal agree on 0:
! the branch rows print byte 00 and about half of them print it as
! "CO".
!
! ---------------------------------------------------------------
! THE CARD SERIALS
! ---------------------------------------------------------------
! LA000056 through LA000110, one prefix for the whole page, no
! break.  ONE REPEAT: LA000101 on line 46 ("KCOP KVI,3,16.32") AND
! line 47 ("BXH,MOPCI"), confirmed at 1200 dpi against LA000100
! above and LA000102 below.  Two statements, one card.
!
! THIS IS A SIXTH INSTANCE OF THE PATTERN printed p.172 NAMED, AND
! IT CORROBORATES RATHER THAN KILLS IT: p.172 observed that in
! every repeated-serial pair the SECOND printed line is a BRANCH
! (four instances on pp.171-172, a fifth on p.148), and line 47 is
! BXH, a branch.  The named killer -- a repeated serial whose
! second line is not a branch -- has still not been seen.  What is
! NEW here is that the FIRST line of the pair is a KVI and not a
! SIC or an LVI, so the pattern is not specific to SIC/branch.
! Nobody should promote it to a rule; the mechanism (whether STRAP
! punches two statements on one card or the listing expands one) is
! a question about C28-6129 and is not settled by any page.
!
! ---------------------------------------------------------------
! THE LOCATION-COLUMN ASTERISK
! ---------------------------------------------------------------
! THREE on this page: line 1 (220742.00, an unlabelled full-word
! VFL store), line 23 (220755.40, an unlabelled half-word branch)
! and line 46 (220771.00, the LABELLED row "KCOP").  Recorded and
! NOTHING PROPOSED.  The workflow says the mark has eight things it
! is not and that a rule proposed from one page was refuted the
! same afternoon.  What this page adds to the record is that the
! three marked rows have nothing in common with each other: one
! labelled and two not, one full word and two half words, one VFL
! and two branches, and the twenty-five other half-word branches
! between lines 5 and 30 are unmarked.
!
