! >>> SUBSTITUTIONS.  THREE, ALL FORCED BY KNOWN ASSEMBLER GAPS,
!     ALL FLAGGED AT THEIR ROW. <<<
! ---------------------------------------------------------------
! (S1) LINE 2's NAME FIELD IS PRINTED "K OP OK" WITH BLANKS and
!      strap_asm refuses a blank in the label field.  Written
!      "KOPOK".  The page itself prints the closed-up spelling on
!      lines 49, 50 and 52, so the substitution is to a spelling
!      THIS PAGE ALSO PRINTS, not to an invention.
! (S2) LINE 15 IS PRINTED "B,R 1+1.0" and (S3) LINE 16 IS PRINTED
!      "B,R 1+2.0" -- a blank inside a name INSIDE AN EXPRESSION,
!      which strap_asm refuses ("undefined symbol 'R'").  Written
!      "B,R1+1.0" and "B,R1+2.0".
!      NOTE THE ASYMMETRY, because it is a finding: LINE 14's
!      "B,R 1" IS WRITTEN AS PRINTED and assembles, because the
!      bare blanked name resolves.  Only the expression form fails.
!      The manual's table prints the same three operands as "R1",
!      "R1+1.0", "R1+2.0", so the substitution agrees with the
!      typeset source as well.
! Every other blanked operand on the page is written AS PRINTED --
! "B,Z START", "B,K S LOC", "B,M OP CI", "SV,2,S TIC" and twenty
! more all assemble unchanged.
!
! ---------------------------------------------------------------
! WHAT COULD NOT BE SETTLED
! ---------------------------------------------------------------
! (A) THE BIT OFFSETS WITHIN THE HALF WORD of all thirty-four
!     external symbols listed above.  There is no SIC on this page,
!     and a branch sees only bit 32 (workflow item 1), so the ".0"
!     and ".40" below are the house convention for twenty-seven of
!     them and a READING only of bit 32.  A passing !CHECK must not
!     be read as a reading.  The seven forward ones -- BTIFR,
!     BRLFR, BRLNR, BKLNR, WGONG, ZTIME, JCOMM -- are not checked
!     against any defining card at all yet.
!
! (B) WHAT THE NAMES MEAN.  "KCOP", "KPLUG1" and "KOPOK" are read
!     as strings and nothing is claimed about what K, C, OP or PLUG
!     stand for.  The manual uses all three as bare labels.
!
! (C) WHETHER LINE 53's "B,MOPCI" IS REALLY THE 13.32 ENTRY.  The
!     arithmetic puts line 53 at displacement 13.32 in KCOP's
!     table, and the manual's footnote says every asterisked
!     routine resets $3 to 13.32 and goes to RALLPS -- but line 53
!     branches to MOPCI, not RALLPS, and line 30 (13.32 in KOPOK's
!     table) is the one that branches to RALLPS.  Both readings are
!     certain from the binary; what the two 13.32 slots are FOR is
!     not established here and is a question for whoever
!     transcribes RALLPS's page.
!
! (D) WHY LINES 1, 23 AND 46 CARRY THE LOCATION-COLUMN ASTERISK.
!     See above.  No hypothesis offered.
!
! (E) WHETHER $ATID 17.0 -> SCBALT EXISTS IN THIS BUILD.  The -1
!     manual lists it; KVI,3,16.32 on line 46 bounds this table at
!     16.32, and the OCR of printed p.179 shows a new routine
!     starting at 221000.00 where a 17.0 entry would have to sit.
!     The evidence says NO, but it rests on a bound and on another
!     page's OCR, so p.179's transcriber should settle it.
!
! ---------------------------------------------------------------
! WHAT WAS RUN, AND WHAT IT SAID
! ---------------------------------------------------------------
!   verify_mcp_page.py 178 -- "3 symbols, 56 listing rows", ALL
!     PASSED.  Fifty-six !CHECK rows for fifty-six located lines,
!     so nothing on the page is unchecked.
!   check_deck_listing_comments.py over a copy of decks/ with this
!     deck added -- reach went from 109 to 110 decks, rows parsed
!     from 3799 to 3855 (+56) and checks compared from 2706 to 2762
!     (+56), with NO new mismatch.  The two failures it reports are
!     printed p.171's and are present in the baseline without this
!     deck; they are not this page's.
!   check_symbol_spellings.py over the same copy -- "PASS 1467
!     symbol definitions, no symbol spelled two ways".
!   >>> check_mcp_body_image.py WITH FIRST,LAST = 99,178 OVER THE
!     SAME COPY -- THE MERGE PASSED. <<<  "merges_without_
!     disagreement = 698 defined, 69 external", against the
!     baseline's 695 and 62: the three new definitions are KOPOK,
!     KPLUG1 and KCOP and the seven new externals are the seven
!     forward stand-ins.  SO ALL THIRTY-FOUR EXTERNAL SYNs ABOVE
!     WERE PUT BESIDE THE CARDS THAT DEFINE THEM AND NONE
!     DISAGREED.  every_word_accounted_for = 0.
!
!     ONE CHECK FAILED AND IT IS NOT THIS PAGE: "UNEXPECTED
!     SLC-covered holes ... 0o220700 ... 0o220713", 34 words,
!     exactly 0o220742 - 0o220700.  Those are printed p.177's
!     words, and p.177 has no deck yet, so this deck's hard origin
!     SLC jumps them.  That is precisely the failure mode the
!     test's own comment names -- "a page LOST from the list ... is
!     jumped over by the NEXT deck's origin SLC" -- and it is the
!     test doing its job.  IT CLOSES WHEN p.177 LANDS, and if it
!     does not close then, exactly 34 words are missing between the
!     two pages and that is where to look.
!
! ===============================================================
