!CHECK 220742.00 | 000003.22 8D 007000.20 D0 | line 1 ST(BU,7),SCW+.18($13) -- THE PAGE'S ONLY FULL WORD and its only location-column asterisk on an unlabelled VFL row.  "SCW+.18" prints 0o22 = 18 DECIMAL, which pins SCW to the BIT at 000003.00, the value printed p.102 line 14 defines.  >>> THE SECOND BYTE IS D0 AND NOT C0: at 1200 dpi this glyph has the same straight vertical left stem and square corners as the D of this row's own "8D", with the bowl worn through on the right; the 400/600-dpi reading was C0 and was wrong.  The low nibble 0 is the absence of an OFFSET index on the second operand
!CHECK 220743.00 | 000002.05 05 | line 2 KOPOK V+I,2,2.0 -- the datum 2.0 words is 0o2 and .05 is 2J+1 for J=2.  >>> THE NAME IS PRINTED "K OP OK" WITH BLANKS and is written closed up here (S1); lines 49/50/52 print the closed-up spelling on this same page
!CHECK 220743.40 | 215265.05 30 | line 3 SV,2,S TIC -- .05 is 2J+1 for J=2, so STIC is checked to the HALF WORD only; twenty-six landed decks already SYN it at 215265.0
!CHECK 220744.00 | 777777.14 03 | line 4 BR,-1.0($3) -- -1.0 is -64 bits, 2^24-64, printing word 0o777777 with bit 0, so the printed 0o14 is BR's OWN operation bits and nothing of the address.  That is this page's calibration of BR, and lines 33 and 48 use it
!CHECK 220744.40 | 217544.10 00 | line 5 B,Z START -READ -- ZSTART at 217544.00 with bit 32 CLEAR, printing the branch's 0o10.  Displacement 1.0 in the manual's $OPS table
