!CHECK 220751.00 | 220120.50 00 | line 14 B,R 1 -SPACE BLOCK -- R1 at 220120.40, CONFIRMING the 220120.50 taken from the volume OCR.  WRITTEN AS PRINTED, blank and all: a bare blanked name resolves, and only the expression forms on lines 15-16 do not
!CHECK 220751.40 | 220121.50 00 | line 15 B,R 1+1.0 -BACKSPACE BLOCK -- R1 + one word; >>> SUBSTITUTED (S2) to "B,R1+1.0", because a blank inside a name inside an expression is refused.  The manual's table prints this operand as "R1+1.0"
!CHECK 220752.00 | 220122.50 00 | line 16 B,R 1+2.0 -SPACE FILE -- R1 + two words; >>> SUBSTITUTED (S3) to "B,R1+2.0", same reason.  Lines 14-16 are one symbol at three offsets, so each is the others' control
!CHECK 220752.40 | 220123.50 00 | line 17 B,R2-.32 -- R2 at 220124.00 minus 32 bits is 220123.40, printing 0o40 OR the branch's 0o10.  THIS ROW IS THE PAGE'S CONTROL ON THE SIGN AND ON THE DECIMAL BIT OFFSET: -.32 DECIMAL is -0o40, and read octal the row would land a half word out.  The manual's table prints the same operand, "R2 - .32"
