!CHECK 220760.40 | 217355.50 00 | line 29 B,JZIOR -- JZIOR at 217355.40, printed p.146's definition; manual $IODEF 13.0, the last entry of the base revision's table
!CHECK 220761.00 | 220346.10 00 | line 30 B,RALLPS -- RALLPS at 220346.00, printed p.167's definition.  THIS IS DISPLACEMENT 13.32, the slot the -1 manual's footnote names: "each routine resets $3 to 13.32 and control goes to RALLPS"
!CHECK 220761.40 | 000045.47 04 | line 31 KPLUG1 KVI,3,37.32 -- the bound 37.32 is 0o45 words plus 0o40 bits, and .47 is 0o40 OR 2J+1 = 7 for J=3.  Read octal the word part would be wrong, so this row pins the DECIMAL reading of both halves.  Printed p.177 line 11 branches here and the volume OCR of that page prints 220761.72 40, which is 0o40 OR BZXL's 0o32 -- an independent reading of this label's half word from another page
!CHECK 220762.00 | 215630.73 42 | line 32 BXH,M OP CI -- MOPCI at 215630.40, printing 0o40 OR BXH's own 0o33; byte 42.  BIT-IDENTICAL TO LINE 47, which prints the same card with the name closed up as "MOPCI" -- one page, one instruction, the blanks varied and nothing else, which is this page's proof that STRAP ignores blanks inside a symbol
!CHECK 220762.40 | 777740.14 03 | line 33 BR,-32.0($3) -- -32 words is 2^24-2048, word 0o777740 bit 0, plus BR's 0o14 as line 4 establishes.  The next half word is 220763.00, so $3 = 32.0 lands on line 34 and $3 = 37.32 on line 45: twelve entries, exactly the bound line 31 sets
!CHECK 220763.00 | 220410.50 00 | line 34 B,K SIO -STACK I/O INTERRUPTS -- KSIO at 220410.40, printed p.170's definition; manual $SIO 32.0.  The volume OCR reads this name "K STO" and it is K SIO
!CHECK 220763.40 | 220415.10 00 | line 35 B,K RIO -RELEASE I/O INTERRUPTS -- KRIO at 220415.00, printed p.170's definition; manual $RIO 32.32
!CHECK 220764.00 | 217154.10 00 | line 36 B,C RETN -RETURN AFTER I/O INTERRUPT -- CRETN at 217154.00, printed p.140's definition; manual $RET 33.0
!CHECK 220764.40 | 217326.10 00 | line 37 B,WRAMPP -RETURN AFTER MASKABLE -- WRAMPP at 217326.00, printed p.144's definition; manual $RAM 33.32
!CHECK 220765.00 | 220427.50 00 | line 38 B,K STRG -STORE IN COMMUNICATION REGION -- KSTRG at 220427.40, CONFIRMING the 220427.50 taken from the volume OCR; the OCR reads the name "K STRGE" and it is K STRG, which printed p.171 defines and the manual prints as $STRG 34.0
!CHECK 220765.40 | 220445.50 00 | line 39 B,K FECRG -FETCH FROM COMMUNICATION REGION -- KFECRG at 220445.40, CONFIRMING the 220445.50 taken from the volume OCR; manual $FECRG 34.32
!CHECK 220766.00 | 233107.10 00 | line 40 B,ZTIME -- ZTIME at 233107.00, a FORWARD stand-in nearly five thousand words past the end of the transcribed body; manual $TIME 35.0
!CHECK 220766.40 | 233154.10 00 | line 41 B,JCOMM -- JCOMM at 233154.00, the same far-forward block as line 40; manual $COMM 35.32.  0o233154 - 0o233107 = 0o45, so the two are 37 words apart and that difference is READ, not assumed
!CHECK 220767.00 | 217347.50 00 | line 42 B,JSITX -SET INTERVAL TIMER -- JSITX at 217347.40, printed p.145's definition; manual $SIT 36.0, the last entry of the base revision's $OPS table
!CHECK 220767.40 | 220560.10 00 | line 43 B,FFXP -- FFXP at 220560.00, CONFIRMING the 220560.10 taken from the volume OCR; printed p.174 defines it ("printed name F FXP").  THE -1 MANUAL PUTS "*SCBTT" IN THIS SLOT, so the listing and the manual differ here and the listing wins for the listing
!CHECK 220770.00 | 220502.10 00 | line 44 B,TSTLR -- TSTLR at 220502.00, CONFIRMING the 220502.10 taken from the volume OCR; printed p.172's own deck quotes this very row as an independent reading of its origin word.  Manual $STLR 37.0
!CHECK 220770.40 | 220523.50 00 | line 45 B,TFCHLR -- TFCHLR at 220523.40, CONFIRMING the 220523.50 taken from the volume OCR; printed p.173 defines it.  Manual $FELR 37.32, the last entry this build's KPLUG1 table reaches
!CHECK 220771.00 | 000020.47 04 | line 46 KCOP KVI,3,16.32 -- the bound 16.32 is 0o20 words plus 0o40 bits, .47 being 0o40 OR 2J+1 = 7 for J=3; the same instruction as line 31 with a different datum, so the pair is each other's control.  Card LA000101, shared with line 47.  CARRIES A LOCATION-COLUMN ASTERISK.  printed p.177 line 43 branches here and prints 220771.32 40, bit 32 CLEAR, an independent reading of this label from another page
!CHECK 220771.40 | 215630.73 42 | line 47 BXH,MOPCI -- bit-identical to line 32; see that row.  Card LA000101, shared with line 46, and this is the BRANCH half of the pair, which is the sixth instance of printed p.172's repeated-serial observation
!CHECK 220772.00 | 777764.54 03 | line 48 BR,-11.32($3) -- -(11*64+32) bits is 2^24-736, word 0o777764 bit 0o40, plus BR's 0o14 giving 0o54.  The next half word is 220772.40, so $3 = 11.32 lands on line 49 and $3 = 16.32 on 220777.40, which is printed p.179's third row.  This row is where the sign, the decimal word part AND the decimal bit part are all checked at once
!CHECK 220772.40 | 220743.10 00 | line 49 B,KOPOK -- this page's own line 2, 220743.00, bit 32 clear.  >>> ONE OF THE THREE IDENTICAL CARDS (49, 50, 52) THAT SETTLE THE NAME: in the FOURTH character position line 50 prints a closed O and this row prints it open, same drum, same column, same instruction
!CHECK 220773.00 | 220743.10 00 | line 50 B,KOPOK -- bit-identical to line 49; the row whose fourth glyph is CLOSED
!CHECK 220773.40 | 220727.50 00 | line 51 B,KNI+1.0 -- KNI at 220726.40 plus one word is 220727.40, printing 0o40 OR 0o10.  KNI is defined on printed p.177 line 42 and printed p.167's deck already SYNs it at 220726.40, so this row corroborates a value it does not establish
!CHECK 220774.00 | 220743.10 00 | line 52 B,KOPOK -- bit-identical to lines 49 and 50, the third of the three
!CHECK 220774.40 | 215630.50 00 | line 53 B,MOPCI -- MOPCI at 215630.40; bit-identical to line 12, which prints the name with blanks.  On this row the name prints its SECOND glyph as an open O and its FOURTH as a genuine C, which is the workflow's "ink varies per CHARACTER, not per row" inside one five-letter name
!CHECK 220775.00 | 220325.10 00 | line 54 B,RHD -- RHD at 220325.00, printed p.167's definition; manual $HD 14.0, the first of the asterisked density/mode entries KCOP serves
!CHECK 220775.40 | 220326.10 00 | line 55 B,RLD -- RLD at 220326.00, one word past RHD, printed p.167's definition; manual $LD 14.32
!CHECK 220776.00 | 220334.50 00 | line 56 B,REVEN -- REVEN at 220334.40, printed p.167's definition; manual $EVEN 15.0.  A HALF WORD, so THE COUNTER LEAVES THIS PAGE AT 220776.40, which is where printed p.179's "B,RODD" must print
